---
id: contact-list
---

Pick one person from a list. A radio group whose options are ContactOption
rows: the list owns selection and keyboard navigation, each row shows one
Contact.

## Visual Contract

<Page>
  <Component name="ContactList" status="stable" implements="hwc-radio-group"
    layoutMode="VERTICAL" primaryAxisSizingMode="AUTO" itemSpacing="{space#xs}" width={280}>
    <Repeat slot="option" count={3}>
      <Instance name="row" component="ContactOption" layoutAlign="STRETCH" />
    </Repeat>
    <Slot name="empty">
      <Text name="nobody" characters="No contacts yet" fontSize={13} fills="{text#muted}" />
    </Slot>
  </Component>
</Page>

<Styles>
  <Style state="disabled" root:opacity="{opacity#disabled}" />
</Styles>

## Contract

<Props>
  <Prop name="items" type="Contact[]">The people to choose from, in order.</Prop>
  <Prop name="name" type="string">Form field name shared by every option.</Prop>
  <Prop name="disabled" type="boolean" default={false} visual>Every option inert.</Prop>
</Props>
<States structural={[]} styling={['disabled']} />
<Slots>
  <Slot name="option" repeats model="{models#Contact}" accepts="hwc-radio">One option per element of `items`.</Slot>
  <Slot name="empty">Shown instead of the options while `items` is empty.</Slot>
</Slots>
<Accessibility role="radiogroup" keyboard="Arrow keys move the choice" />
<Composes with="ContactOption, Field" />

## Models

<Model name="Contact">
  One person as a row shows them. Every value is display-ready; the adapter that builds it does any formatting.
  <Field name="id" type="string" key sample={['ada', 'grace', 'linus']}>Stable identity, used for keys and as the submitted value.</Field>
  <Field name="name" type="string" sample={['Ada Lovelace', 'Grace Hopper', 'Linus Torvalds']}>Full display name.</Field>
  <Field name="email" type="string" optional sample={['ada@example.com', null, 'linus@example.com']}>Omitted when unknown; the row hides the line.</Field>
</Model>

## Behavior

- one-choice: exactly one option is chosen at a time; choosing one unchooses the rest.
- keyboard: arrow keys move the choice through the options; Tab leaves the group.
- empty: with no items the `empty` slot shows and nothing is chosen.

## Examples

<Example name="second-chosen">
  <Set slot="option" count={3} />
  <Set at="option[1]" state="checked" />
</Example>
